; shr_amount_at_or_above_word_size: the SHR mirror of
; shl_amount_at_or_above_word_size.
;
; This is the starker half. `8 >> 64` computed in unbounded integers is 0,
; well inside the i64 range, so it never reaches any overflow check: a VM
; that relied on one would complete with 0 on the stack instead of raising
; InvalidShift. No overflow is involved, so nothing in the arithmetic
; sweep could find it.

PUSH 8
PUSH 64
SHR
HALT
